    <!-- How to fly -->
    <string name="help_title">How to fly</string>
    <string name="help_subtitle">Both sticks spring back to the middle when you let go.</string>
    <string name="help_left_title">Left stick</string>
    <string name="help_left_up">Up: climb</string>
    <string name="help_left_down">Middle or below: motors off</string>
    <string name="help_left_left">Turn left</string>
    <string name="help_left_right">Turn right</string>
    <string name="help_left_note">Push up slowly until the drone lifts. Let go and the motors stop, so keep your thumb on it.</string>
    <string name="help_right_title">Right stick</string>
    <string name="help_right_up">Up: fly forward</string>
    <string name="help_right_down">Down: fly back</string>
    <string name="help_right_left">Slide left</string>
    <string name="help_right_right">Slide right</string>
    <string name="help_right_note">Small movements go a long way. Let go and the drone levels out.</string>
    <string name="help_steps_title">Before you take off</string>
    <string name="help_steps" formatted="false">1.  Put the drone on flat ground and switch it on. Don\'t touch it for 3 seconds while the sensors settle.\n2.  Tap Connect. The phone joins the drone\'s Wi-Fi on its own (allow it the first time). Battery and signal show up at the top.\n3.  Let go of the left stick and tap Arm. The button turns amber: the drone is live.\n4.  Ease the left stick up until it lifts off, then steer with the right stick.\n5.  To land, lower the left stick slowly or tap Land. Land at 20% battery or when the timer shows under a minute.\n6.  Tap Disarm once it\'s on the ground.</string>
    <string name="help_buttons_title">Buttons</string>
    <string name="help_buttons" formatted="false">Arm / Disarm (top): the motors can only spin while armed. Let go of the left stick before arming. If it sits on the ground armed for 20 seconds, or the phone disconnects, it disarms itself.\nLand: the drone levels itself, sinks to the ground and disarms. Tap Cancel to take back control.\nHold to stop: press and hold for half a second to cut the motors at once. Emergencies only, the drone will drop.\nTimer (next to battery): roughly how many minutes of flying are left.\nLock (on the left stick): stops the left stick moving sideways, so you can\'t turn by accident.\nLive, Photo, Record: camera feed, photos and video. These need a XIAO ESP32-S3 Sense running this firmware.\nIf the Wi-Fi signal drops for half a second, the drone lands by itself.\nWarnings: the phone buzzes and a banner shows at 25% and 15% battery.\nGear: flying style (Beginner, Normal, Sport), motor test, level calibration, find my drone, Wi-Fi password and firmware updates.\nHeight sensor (VL53L1X on a Qwiic port): the drone holds its height by itself, the stick centre means hover, and Land becomes Take off while on the ground.</string>
    <string name="help_mode_note">These are Mode 2 controls (the default). You can swap sticks in Settings, Flight control, Mode.</string>
    <string name="help_done">Got it</string>

